The program also uses a custom logging mechanism to categorize and log different types of errors. The `Logging` class defines an `ErrorType` enum class with three error types: `NETWORK`, `PARSING`, and `INTERNAL_PROCESSING`. The `log()` function takes a string message and an `ErrorType` object as input, and logs the message to the console.

The `WorkerThread` class is used to handle GET requests concurrently using worker threads. Each thread in the pool handles one request at a time, and updates metrics such as successful requests, failed requests, total response time, and peak active sessions. The `handleRequest()` function implements the request handling logic, and updates the metrics accordingly.

The `SandeshClient` class is used to create an instance of the Sandesh client using the io_service object. The `start()` function starts the server connection and runs indefinitely, gracefully handling interruptions and cleaning up resources. The program uses a test double for the `InterfaceTable` class and overrides the `FindVmUuidFromMetadataIp` function to return a random UUID based on a hash of the input IP address.

The main function creates an instance of the Sandesh client using the io_service object, and starts the server connection and runs indefinitely, gracefully handling interruptions and cleaning up resources.']

