This code uses the `requests` library to fetch images from external sources and stores them in a local cache directory. It also verifies the integrity of the cached images by comparing checksums before using them in the application. The `ImageManager` class has a single method, `load_image`, which takes an image URL as input and returns an `Image` object. If the image is already cached, it loads it from the cache directory. Otherwise, it fetches the image from the external source, stores it in the cache directory, and verifies its integrity by comparing checksums. The `_get_cache_file` method is used to generate a unique file name for each image based on its URL.']

