The `TrafficMonitor` class is responsible for fetching data from all APIs, updating the cache, and getting the latest data. It also allows the user to adjust the resolution and refresh rate of the dashboard.

The `API` class represents a single third-party API, and has methods for fetching data, updating the cache, and getting the latest data.

The `main` function is responsible for running the traffic monitoring application in an infinite loop, fetching data from all APIs, updating the cache, and printing the latest data to the console. It also allows the user to adjust the resolution and refresh rate of the dashboard based on their preferences specified in a JSON configuration file.

The code uses the `json` library to load the JSON configuration file and parse it into a dictionary. The `requests` library is used to fetch data from the APIs, and the `time` library is used to sleep for the appropriate amount of time between API calls.

