1. Validates the input parameters to prevent resource exhaustion and ensures that the number of tasks does not exceed the maximum limit.
2. Allocates memory for the task cache and initializes it with the input tasks.
3. Randomly assigns a status to each task based on a probabilistic model that simulates real-world task completion rates. The function implements a mechanism to retry tasks that fail within the specified timeout period, up to a maximum number of retries. Retry logic considers the elapsed time since the last attempt and adjusts the retry interval dynamically using the backoff strategy.
