The implementation also uses thread-safe memory management and concurrency control to handle simultaneous access from multiple threads without causing data corruption. The mutex lock is used to ensure that only one thread can access the queue at a time, preventing race conditions and ensuring that the queue remains consistent.

Finally, the implementation includes error handling and resource cleanup mechanisms to ensure robustness under various input conditions. For example, if the external configuration service is slow or unresponsive, the `handleExternalConfigService` function can be used to implement strategies to mitigate the impact on overall system performance. Similarly, the `readJsonFile` and `writeOutputFile` functions include error handling mechanisms to ensure that the queue remains consistent even in case of errors during file I/O operations.

Overall, this implementation is designed to be efficient in terms of both memory usage and access speed, while maintaining code maintainability and ease of integration into existing systems. It can handle up to 10,000 services and millions of messages efficiently, without compromising performance.']

