The function then allocates memory for the report entry array and initializes each entry with the corresponding measurement and sensor data.

Finally, it returns pointers to the allocated arrays and a status indicator. The function also frees all allocated memory when it exits, either normally or due to an error.

This implementation balances memory efficiency, integration complexity, and performance optimization by using standard library functions for memory allocation and de-allocation. It also ensures that the application can recover from allocation failures without crashing by checking for `NULL` pointers before using them. Additionally, it uses a robust file reading mechanism to ensure that the function does not block the main thread and is fault-tolerant.']

