This code uses a struct to store the unique integers and floating-point numbers, as well as the most frequent numerical value across the entire dataset. It also includes functions for dynamically allocating memory for the struct, handling errors during memory allocation, processing the mixed data stream, tracking the total number of unique integers and floating-point numbers, tracking the most frequent numerical value, and periodically flushing intermediate results to a persistent storage solution for auditing and analysis purposes.

The code is designed to be efficient in both time and space, considering edge cases such as all entries being negative, all being positive, or the array being empty. It ignores non-numeric inputs and treats them as missing entries without halting processing. The function also includes robust error handling for memory allocation failures, providing meaningful feedback to the user.

