The `parse_command_line` function initializes command line options and parses the input arguments using `getopt`. It also checks for invalid inputs and displays an error message if any are found. The `process_file` function opens the input file for reading, reads it line by line, and performs operations on each line to count lines, words, and characters. It updates the file statistics and prints them at the end of processing.

The program handles edge cases such as very large files that may exceed available memory, malformed input files, and unexpected command line arguments robustly by providing clear and actionable error messages. It also implements a mechanism to monitor and report on resource usage, which can aid in debugging and optimization efforts.']

