Once the entire file has been read, the function identifies and prints the largest integer in the list using a simple loop that iterates over the values in the list and compares each value to the current largest value. The `largest` variable is initialized to 0 and updated as needed during the loop.

Finally, the function frees the memory allocated for the integer list using `free()` and returns 0 to indicate success. If an error occurs during memory allocation or file reading, the function prints an error message using `perror()` and returns -1 to indicate failure.']

['```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.logging.*;

public class ConfigurationManager {
    private static final Logger LOGGER = Logger.getLogger(ConfigurationManager.class.getName());

    // Custom memory pool with configurable size and automatic resizing
    private static final MemoryPool<Configuration> POOL = new MemoryPool<>();

    // Map of configurations by service name
    private static final Map<String, Configuration> CONFIGURATIONS = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    // Cache of recently accessed configurations
    private static final Map<String, Configuration> CACHE = new LRUCache<>();

    // Synchronization mechanism for concurrent access to the configuration map
    private static final Object LOCK = new Object();

    public static void addConfiguration(String serviceName, String version, String environment) {
        synchronized (LOCK) {
            Configuration configuration = new Configuration(serviceName, version, environment);
            CONFIGURATIONS.put(serviceName, configuration);
            CACHE.put(serviceName, configuration);
        }
    }

    public static void updateConfiguration(String serviceName, String version, String environment) {
        synchronized (LOCK) {
            Configuration configuration = CONFIGURATIONS.get(serviceName);
            if (configuration != null) {
                configuration.setVersion(version);
                configuration.setEnvironment(environment);
                CACHE.put(serviceName, configuration);
            } else {
                LOGGER.warning("Attempted to update non-existent configuration for service " + serviceName);
            }
        }
    }

    public static Configuration getConfiguration(String serviceName) {
        synchronized (LOCK) {
            Configuration configuration = CACHE.get(serviceName);
            if (configuration == null) {
                configuration = CONFIGURATIONS.get(serviceName);
                if (configuration != null) {
                    CACHE.put(serviceName, configuration);
                }
            }
            return configuration;
        }
    }

    public static void removeConfiguration(String serviceName) {
        synchronized (LOCK) {
            CONFIGURATIONS.remove(serviceName);
            CACHE.remove(serviceName);
        }
    }

    private static class Configuration {
        private String serviceName;
        private String version;
        private String environment;

        public Configuration(String serviceName, String version, String environment) {
            this.serviceName = serviceName;
            this.version = version;
            this.environment = environment;
        }

        public void setVersion(String version) {
            this.version = version;
        }

        public void setEnvironment(String environment) {
            this.environment = environment;
        }

        public String getServiceName() {
            return serviceName;
        }

        public String getVersion() {
            return version;
        }

        public String getEnvironment() {
            return environment;
        }
    }
}
```
