This code example demonstrates how to implement a list data structure in C that can be used to store and manage TIDB_ROW_RECORD structures. The list is designed to be thread-safe, with mutex locks used to ensure that concurrent accesses do not cause race conditions or other issues. The list also includes mechanisms for tracking and limiting the maximum number of records that can be added to the list, preventing overflow. Additionally, the list supports dynamic resizing to accommodate increasing loads without excessive memory overhead.

