The function uses `rand()` to generate random numbers within the specified range `[min_value, max_value]`, which is used to initialize the `value` field in each `record` structure. The `time(NULL)` function is used to get the current timestamp, which is used to determine when an object is expired and needs to be evicted from the cache.

