The `update_in_list()` function is used to update existing instances of the `NetworkInterfaceStats` or `SensorReading` structures in the linked list. It iterates through the linked list until it finds a match for the input data, then updates the data field of the node with the new data. If no match is found, it prints an error message.

The `get_stats()` function is used to retrieve aggregated statistics for all instances of the `NetworkInterfaceStats` and `SensorReading` structures in the linked list. It iterates through the linked list and calculates the aggregated statistics for each data structure.

The `export_to_file()` function is used to export the statistics/readings to a file in CSV or JSON format. It opens the output file for writing, then iterates through the linked list and writes the data to the output file in CSV or JSON format.

The `manage_memory()` function is used to manage memory allocation and deallocation for the linked list. It frees any dynamically allocated memory that is no longer needed.

The `validate_list()` function is used to validate the correctness of the linked list structure at periodic intervals. It iterates through the linked list and checks for any inconsistencies or discrepancies in the data field of each node, as well as gaps in the linked list.

The `concurrent_access()` function is used to implement concurrency support for the linked list. It uses a mutex to synchronize access to the linked list from multiple threads, then iterates through the linked list and performs any necessary operations on the data field of each node.

