This code implements a connection pool for a high-load web service application. The pool is initialized with a fixed size and an idle timeout, which determines how long a connection can remain open before it is closed. The pool also includes a load-based connection prioritization feature that allocates resources to higher-priority connections first.

The code uses a mutex to ensure thread-safe operations when handling concurrent access from multiple threads attempting to open, close, or query connections. It also includes an idling mechanism to close connections after a specified period of inactivity, balancing between maintaining resource efficiency and data integrity.

To adjust the parameters dynamically without affecting ongoing operations, the code uses a flexible configuration mechanism that allows loading the configuration from a file. The configuration can be updated at runtime by reloading the file.

The solution is designed to scale to handle an increased number of concurrent connections and maintain consistent performance under heavy load. It also ensures thread-safe operations and balances between resource efficiency and data integrity.']

