The code uses a `configuration_key` structure to store the unique key ID, a reference to a shared `resource` structure, and a `last_modified_timestamp` to track changes. The system also includes an `invalidate_outdated_configs()` function that invalidates outdated configurations automatically, ensuring efficient resource usage and optimal performance under high concurrency.

The code also includes error handling and logging mechanisms to manage failures gracefully and provide detailed logging and notifications when errors occur. The system can be scaled horizontally by supporting seamless integration with distributed systems and cloud environments.']

