            String[] fields = line.split(",");
            if (fields.length < 3) continue;
            String name = fields[0];
            String type = fields[1];
            int level = Integer.parseInt(fields[2]);

            // Determine Pokemon weaknesses based on its type
            switch (type) {
                case "Fire":
                    writer.println("Weak to Water");
                    break;
                case "Water":
                    writer.println("Weak to Fire");
                    break;
                case "Grass":
                    writer.println("Weak to Poison");
                    break;
                case "Poison":
                    writer.println("Weak to Grass");
                    break;
            }

            // Write results to output file
            writer.println(name + ", level " + level);
        }

        // Close input and output files
        reader.close();
        if (writer != null) {
            writer.close();
        }
    }
}
```
This program uses the `BufferedReader` class to read lines from the input file, and the `PrintWriter` class to write results to the output file. It also uses the `String.split()` method to parse each line of the input file into its component fields, and the `Integer.parseInt()` method to convert the level field to an integer.

The program determines the weaknesses of each Pokemon based on its type using a switch statement. It retrieves the type information from a library function and the Pokemon's name from another library function. The results are then written to the output file using the `PrintWriter` class.

