The `network_interface_stats_array_add()` function adds a new network interface statistics to the dynamic array. It first acquires the mutex lock, then checks if the array needs to be resized by comparing the current capacity with the number of elements in the array. If necessary, it reallocates the memory for the array and updates the capacity. Finally, it adds the new network interface statistics to the end of the array and releases the mutex lock.

The `network_interface_stats_array_update()` function updates an existing network interface statistics in the dynamic array. It first acquires the mutex lock, then finds the index of the existing statistics in the array using a linear search. If the index is found, it updates the existing statistics with the new values. Otherwise, it adds the new statistics to the end of the array. Finally, it releases the mutex lock.

The `network_interface_stats_array_get_aggregate()` function retrieves aggregated statistics for all interfaces in the dynamic array. It first acquires the mutex lock, then initializes an aggregate structure with zero values. Then, it iterates over all interfaces in the array and updates the aggregate statistics with the current values. Finally, it releases the mutex lock and returns the aggregate statistics.

