To handle potential race conditions when multiple threads attempt to schedule and update project tasks concurrently, this implementation uses a lock on the mutex to ensure that only one thread can access the registry at a time. This ensures that the integrity of the data is maintained across all threads.

To automatically reassign overdue tasks to a backup team in case of team member unavailability, this implementation uses a sliding window cache to store the availability and status of each team member. The cache is updated periodically using an external API for fetching real-time team availability and project statuses. This ensures that the cache remains up-to-date without introducing significant overhead in terms of frequency of API calls.

To handle dependencies efficiently, this implementation uses a hybrid approach combining hash tables and linked lists to manage project dependencies. The hash table is used to quickly find projects that are dependent on a given project, while the linked list is used to maintain the order of dependencies. This allows for efficient handling of dependencies without introducing significant overhead in terms of memory usage or processing times.

